rl":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent","html_url":"https://github.com/pafuent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T19:51:21Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T19:51:21Z","body":"> Also when deleting single file, the item list is scrollable by a pixel\r\n\r\n@KoBeWi I tried a lot of different things trying to know the size of one tree item to set the minimum size of the tree. My plan was to have the size of 5 items as max (for less items just set it to see all the items)\r\nThe best approximation are this lines:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (tree_item_count > 0) {\r\n\tconst uint32_t multiplier = MIN(tree_item_count, 5);\r\n\towners->set_custom_minimum_size(Size2(0, 35 * multiplier) * EDSCALE);\r\n}\r\n```\r\nIs there a better way to know the exact size of a tree item?\r\n(sadly my knowledge on Godot GUI is limited)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479813561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479999463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98539#issuecomment-2479999463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/i